sections.wikitext:
The song was used during the closing credits of ''[[Asterix & Obelix: Mission Cleopatra]]'' (2002) by Alain Chabat, one of [[List of highest-grossing films in France|the biggest successes]] in French cinema box-office history.{{fact|date=May 2026}}

The song was used in ''[[Totally Spies! The Movie]]'' (2009).<ref>{{cite web|title= Various Artists – Totally Spies Bof |website= [[AllMusic]] |url= http://www.allmusic.com/album/totally-spies-bof-mw0002032761 |accessdate=2015-03-02 }}</ref>

In 2009, in the ''[[Family Guy]]'' episode title "420" (S07 E12), Carter Pewterschmidt is shown listening to the song while singing different lyrics that relate to his life.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Treisman |first=Rachel |date=2023-04-24 |title=Edgy or insensitive? The Paralympics TikTok account sparks a debate |url=https://www.npr.org/2023/04/24/1171333573/paralympics-tiktok-controversy |work=[[NPR News]] |quote=A slow-motion replay of a wheelchair basketball player falling backwards onto the floor is accompanied by the ''Family Guy'' version of "Walk Like An Egyptian" ("My back is hurting from the chair I'm sitting on ... if I lay down flat on the floor it usually kinda fixes it").}}</ref>

In 2012, the song was used in season 3 of ''[[Eastbound & Down]]''.{{fact|date=May 2026}}

In 2014, the song was used as the ending credits theme for the first 24 episodes of the Japanese animated series ''[[JoJo's Bizarre Adventure: Stardust Crusaders]]'', which was based on the [[Stardust Crusaders|third part]] of the manga series ''[[JoJo's Bizarre Adventure]]'', which is set on a travel from Japan to Egypt.<ref>{{cite web|first= Mikikazu |last= Komatsu |title= Pat Metheny Group's 1987 Song "Last Train Home" Featured as New ED Song for "JoJo's Bizarre Adventure" |url= http://www.crunchyroll.com/anime-news/2015/01/09/pat-metheny-groups-1987-song-last-train-home-featured-as-new-ed-song-for-jojos-bizarre-adventure |website=Crunchyroll News |date=2015-01-10 |accessdate=2015-01-22 }}</ref>

The song was performed in the Spanish animated movie ''[[Mummies (2023 film)|Mummies]]'' (2023).{{fact|date=May 2026}}

